    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_6d3e0e937fb86ed9f4f3d74cd916ed99c7e4ee0ae721fb70a39f9fe98a498d00",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Euler-product positivity couples the logarithmic derivatives at heights 0, t, and 2t, while local zero factorization turns any nearby zero into a positive reciprocal-distance term. Growth control sets the localization radius and remainder bound, so the positivity inequality cannot absorb a zero closer to the one-line than a scale proportional to 1/(phi w).",
